    "Either way, you can choose exactly what you hear about under You, Notifications, Outposts." : {
      "comment" : "A description of the notification settings.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Encrypted between people, but built around an account tied to your real identity and a company whose business is knowing about you. %@ has no identity to tie anything to. There are no algorithms and no social media ecosystem to be a part of." : {

    },
    "Encrypted in transit and at rest, WhatsApp is owned by Meta, which sees who you talk to and how often even when it cannot see what you say. That pattern—the words are private, the social graph is not—is what the rotating addresses here are for. Your data is part of the larger Meta ecosystem." : {

